From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 17:26:35 +0200
Subject: media: gc2145: Put unity in the middle of the image control sliders

Contrast and saturation were offered over the full register range, but
unity is 0x40 of 255 for one and 0x20 of 255 for the other, so on a
slider the whole usable range sat in the bottom quarter and the bottom
eighth. Everything above that is chroma and luma that clipped a long
way back, which is why saturation appeared to do all its work in the
first fifth of its travel.

Stop both at twice unity. The controls still carry exactly what goes
into the register.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c | 13 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
@@ -1736,10 +1736,19 @@ static int gc2145_init_controls(struct gc2145_dev *sensor)
 	 */
 	ctrls->brightness = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_BRIGHTNESS,
 					      -128, 127, 1, 0);
+	/*
+	 * Both stop at twice unity rather than at the full register range.
+	 * Unity is 0x40 of 255 for contrast and 0x20 of 255 for saturation,
+	 * so over the whole range the useful part is squeezed into the
+	 * bottom quarter and the bottom eighth, and the rest is chroma and
+	 * luma that clipped long ago. Halving the span puts unity in the
+	 * middle of the slider.
+	 */
 	ctrls->contrast = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_CONTRAST,
-					    0, 255, 1, GC2145_CONTRAST_UNITY);
+					    0, GC2145_CONTRAST_UNITY * 2, 1,
+					    GC2145_CONTRAST_UNITY);
 	ctrls->saturation = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_SATURATION,
-					      0, 255, 1,
+					      0, GC2145_SATURATION_UNITY * 2, 1,
 					      GC2145_SATURATION_UNITY);
 	ctrls->sharpness = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_SHARPNESS,
 					     0, 15, 1, 4);
